  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run `vite build` or open the scene in a browser, so I have not seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Crystals:** Seven crystals are built with `geometry.define`/`geometry.custom`. Each is a 5- or 6-sided prism with a pointed top. They have different heights, radii and tilts. The vertices are not shared between faces, so the shading is flat, and every face has its own colour.\n- **Rotation:** The crystals sit on a dark metallic pedestal disc. Each crystal turns slowly about the pedestal's vertical axis, driven from `app.onFrame`.\n- **Sparks:** Five additive `effects.particles` emitters ring the cluster and one sits at its core. They use the `spark-streak` sprite and drift upward.\n- **Look:** The background is a near-black gradient sky. A dim cool key light, magenta and cyan rim lights from behind, and a violet point light inside the cluster light the crystals. Bloom and a vignette are on.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames. The engine owns the render loop.\n\nParticle direction, spark colour and the sky's `horizonGlow` setting are guesses from the docs. The recipes only show the emitter options I used for upward motion, so the sparks may need tuning once the scene is viewed.\n\n",
